# Build-context exclusions for the image.
#
# Docker sends this whole directory to the daemon before it builds, and every
# file that survives the COPY lands in the image. Neither of the things below
# belongs there.
#
# NOTE: `models/` is deliberately NOT excluded. It is the whole point of the
# build context -- the weights ship inside the image because the container has
# no network at evaluation time. The repository's .gitignore excludes the same
# directory for a different reason (git cannot carry 129 MB), and the two files
# are easy to confuse. Excluding it here would produce an image that builds
# cleanly and then cannot load a model.

# Byte-compiled output from local test runs. A .pyc carries the source mtime and
# size it was built from; if a stale one matches, the interpreter uses it in
# preference to the .py sitting beside it. Not worth the risk for a cache.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Test and tooling caches.
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
